{"id":"mahabharata-12-339","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":339,"title":"एकोनचत्वारिंशदधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 339 · Brahma teaches the eternal Person","summary":{"en":"Brahma tells his son Rudra how the Person is eternal, imperishable, immeasurable and all-pervading, and says that he himself does not know the highest course of him, but speaks as far as his knowledge goes. He tells the many forms of the Person, those bound by action and those freed, and ends the teaching of Sankhya and Yoga.","kn":"ಪುರುಷ ಶಾಶ್ವತ, ಅವ್ಯಯ, ಅಕ್ಷಯ, ಅಪ್ರಮೇಯ, ಸರ್ವವ್ಯಾಪಿ ಎಂದು ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಮಗ ರುದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತನಗೂ ಅವನ ಪರಮ ಗತಿ ತಿಳಿಯದು, ತಿಳಿದಷ್ಟು ಹೇಳುತ್ತೇನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಮಬದ್ಧರು, ಮುಕ್ತರು ಎಂಬ ಪುರುಷನ ಅನೇಕ ರೂಪಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳಿ ಸಾಂಖ್ಯ-ಯೋಗ ಬೋಧನೆ ಮುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"ब्रह्मा पुत्र रुद्र से कहते हैं कि पुरुष शाश्वत, अव्यय, अक्षय, अप्रमेय और सर्वव्यापी है, और कि वे स्वयं उसकी परम गति नहीं जानते, जितना ज्ञान है उतना कहते हैं। वे पुरुष के अनेक रूप, कर्मबद्ध और मुक्त, बताकर सांख्य-योग उपदेश समाप्त करते हैं।","te":"పురుషుడు శాశ్వతుడు, అవ్యయుడు, అక్షయుడు, అప్రమేయుడు, సర్వవ్యాపి అని బ్రహ్మ కొడుకు రుద్రునికి చెబుతాడు; తనకు కూడా ఆయన పరమ గతి తెలియదని, తెలిసినంత చెబుతానని అంటాడు. కర్మబద్ధులు, ముక్తులు అని పురుషుని అనేక రూపాలు చెప్పి సాంఖ్య యోగ బోధనను ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"புருஷன் நிலையானவன், அழியாதவன், அளவற்றவன், எங்கும் பரவியவன் என்று பிரம்மன் மகன் ருத்ரனிடம் கூறி, தனக்கும் அவனுடைய உயர்ந்த கதி தெரியாது, அறிந்தவரை சொல்கிறேன் என்கிறார். செயலால் கட்டுண்டோர், விடுபட்டோர் என்று புருஷனின் பல வடிவங்களைக் கூறிச் சாங்கிய யோகப் போதனையை முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"തന്റെ പുത്രനായ രുദ്രനോട് ബ്രഹ്മാവ് പുരുഷന്റെ ശാശ്വതത്വം, നശിക്കാത്ത സ്വഭാവം, അളക്കാനാവാത്തതും എല്ലായിടത്തും വ്യാപിച്ചതുമായ സ്വഭാവം എന്നിവ പറയുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ഉന്നതമായ വഴി തനിക്ക് അറിയില്ലെന്നും, തന്റെ അറിവിന്റെ പരിധിവരെ മാത്രം സംസാരിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും പറയുന്നു. പുരുഷന്റെ പല രൂപങ്ങളും, കർമ്മത്താൽ ബന്ധിതരും മോചിതരുമായവരെയും വിവരിച്ച് സാംഖ്യത്തിന്റെയും യോഗത്തിന്റെയും ഉപദേശം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.339; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शृणु पुत्र यथा ह्येष पुरुषः शाश्वतोऽव्ययः ।\nअक्षयश्चाप्रमेयश्च सर्वगश्च निरुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, listen to how this Person is described: eternal, imperishable, inexhaustible, immeasurable, and all-pervading."}},{"n":2,"text":"न स शक्यस्त्वया द्रष्टुं मयान्यैर्वापि सत्तम ।\nसगुणो निर्गुणो विश्वो ज्ञानदृश्यो ह्यसौ स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither you, nor I, nor others, good one, can see him; he is said to be with qualities and without, the universe, seen only by knowledge."}},{"n":3,"text":"अशरीरः शरीरेषु सर्वेषु निवसत्यसौ ।\nवसन्नपि शरीरेषु न स लिप्यति कर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without a body, he dwells in all bodies; though dwelling in bodies, he is not stained by actions."}},{"n":4,"text":"ममान्तरात्मा तव च ये चान्ये देहसंज्ञिताः ।\nसर्वेषां साक्षिभूतोऽसौ न ग्राह्यः केनचित्क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the inner self of me and of you and of the others called embodied; the witness of all, he cannot be grasped by anyone anywhere."}},{"n":5,"text":"विश्वमूर्धा विश्वभुजो विश्वपादाक्षिनासिकः ।\nएकश्चरति क्षेत्रेषु स्वैरचारी यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the universe as head and arms, feet, eyes, and nose of the universe, he alone moves in the fields, wandering freely at his pleasure."}},{"n":6,"text":"क्षेत्राणि हि शरीराणि बीजानि च शुभाशुभे ।\nतानि वेत्ति स योगात्मा ततः क्षेत्रज्ञ उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fields are bodies and the seeds are good and bad deeds; he who is the yoga-self knows them, and so is called Kshetrajna."}},{"n":7,"text":"नागतिर्न गतिस्तस्य ज्ञेया भूतेन केनचित् ।\nसांख्येन विधिना चैव योगेन च यथाक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His coming and going can be known by no being, whether by the method of Samkhya or by yoga, in order."}},{"n":8,"text":"चिन्तयामि गतिं चास्य न गतिं वेद्मि चोत्तमाम् ।\nयथाज्ञानं तु वक्ष्यामि पुरुषं तं सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I ponder his course and yet do not know his highest course; but as far as knowledge goes I will speak of that eternal Person."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्यैकत्वं महत्त्वं हि स चैकः पुरुषः स्मृतः ।\nमहापुरुषशब्दं स बिभर्त्येकः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His oneness is his greatness; that one is remembered as the Person. That one eternal being bears the name of the Great Person."}},{"n":10,"text":"एको हुताशो बहुधा समिध्यते\nएकः सूर्यस्तपसां योनिरेका ।\nएको वायुर्बहुधा वाति लोके\nमहोदधिश्चाम्भसां योनिरेकः ।\nपुरुषश्चैको निर्गुणो विश्वरूप-\nस्तं निर्गुणं पुरुषं चाविशन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One fire is kindled in many ways; one sun is the source of heat; one wind blows in many ways in the world; one great ocean is the source of waters; and one Person, without qualities and of universal form, is the one into whom those without qualities enter."}},{"n":11,"text":"हित्वा गुणमयं सर्वं कर्म हित्वा शुभाशुभम् ।\nउभे सत्यानृते त्यक्त्वा एवं भवति निर्गुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up all that is made of qualities, giving up action good and bad, and renouncing both truth and falsehood, one becomes without qualities."}},{"n":12,"text":"अचिन्त्यं चापि तं ज्ञात्वा भावसूक्ष्मं चतुष्टयम् ।\nविचरेद्यो यतिर्यत्तः स गच्छेत्पुरुषं प्रभुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing him as inconceivable, and the four subtle states of being, the ascetic who lives with effort reaches the Person, the Lord."}},{"n":13,"text":"एवं हि परमात्मानं केचिदिच्छन्ति पण्डिताः ।\nएकात्मानं तथात्मानमपरेऽध्यात्मचिन्तकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some learned men thus desire the Supreme Self, and others, who reflect on the self, desire a single Self and the individual self."}},{"n":14,"text":"तत्र यः परमात्मा हि स नित्यं निर्गुणः स्मृतः ।\nस हि नारायणो ज्ञेयः सर्वात्मा पुरुषो हि सः ।\nन लिप्यते फलैश्चापि पद्मपत्रमिवाम्भसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among these, the Supreme Self is remembered as eternally without qualities; he is to be known as Narayana, the self of all, the Person; he is not stained by the fruits of actions, as a lotus leaf is not by water."}},{"n":15,"text":"कर्मात्मा त्वपरो योऽसौ मोक्षबन्धैः स युज्यते ।\nससप्तदशकेनापि राशिना युज्यते हि सः ।\nएवं बहुविधः प्रोक्तः पुरुषस्ते यथाक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The other, the self of action, is bound by liberation and bondage, and is joined with the group of seventeen. Thus the Person has been described to you in his many aspects in order."}},{"n":16,"text":"यत्तत्कृत्स्नं लोकतन्त्रस्य धाम\nवेद्यं परं बोधनीयं सबोद्धृ ।\nमन्ता मन्तव्यं प्राशिता प्राशितव्यं\nघ्राता घ्रेयं स्पर्शिता स्पर्शनीयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That which is the whole abode of the world's machinery, the knowable, the supreme, the one to be awakened with the awakener, the thinker and the thought, the eater and the eaten, the smeller and the smelled, the toucher and the touched,"}},{"n":17,"text":"द्रष्टा द्रष्टव्यं श्राविता श्रावणीयं\nज्ञाता ज्ञेयं सगुणं निर्गुणं च ।\nयद्वै प्रोक्तं गुणसाम्यं प्रधानं\nनित्यं चैतच्छाश्वतं चाव्ययं च ॥","meaning":{"en":"the seer and the seen, the hearer and the heard, the knower and the known, with qualities and without; what is called the balance of qualities, the Pradhana, is eternal, everlasting, and imperishable."}},{"n":18,"text":"यद्वै सूते धातुराद्यं निधानं\nतद्वै विप्राः प्रवदन्तेऽनिरुद्धम् ।\nयद्वै लोके वैदिकं कर्म साधु\nआशीर्युक्तं तद्धि तस्योपभोज्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That which gives birth to the first treasury of the Creator, brahmins call Aniruddha. Whatever Vedic action is rightly done in the world, joined with a wish, is to be enjoyed by him."}},{"n":19,"text":"देवाः सर्वे मुनयः साधु दान्ता-\nस्तं प्राग्यज्ञैर्यज्ञभागं यजन्ते ।\nअहं ब्रह्मा आद्य ईशः प्रजानां\nतस्माज्जातस्त्वं च मत्तः प्रसूतः ।\nमत्तो जगज्जङ्गमं स्थावरं च\nसर्वे वेदाः सरहस्या हि पुत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the gods and sages, rightly self-controlled, worship him with sacrifices as the recipient of the sacrificial share. I, Brahma, am the first lord of creatures; from him I was born, and you were born from me. From me come the world, moving and unmoving, and all the Vedas with their secrets, son."}},{"n":20,"text":"चतुर्विभक्तः पुरुषः स क्रीडति यथेच्छति ।\nएवं स एव भगवाञ्ज्ञानेन प्रतिबोधितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fourfold divided, the Person plays as he pleases; so that same blessed one is awakened by knowledge."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतत्ते कथितं पुत्र यथावदनुपृच्छतः ।\nसांख्यज्ञाने तथा योगे यथावदनुवर्णितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you this, son, as you asked, accurately, as it is described in Samkhya knowledge and in yoga."}}]}]}